{"question":"What is the cardinality of the set of all binary sequences that do not contain the subsequence '10'?",
"justification":"The set in question consists of all binary sequences where once a '1' appears, all subsequent elements must also be '1'. This is because if a '0' appears after a '1', it would form the subsequence '10'. The set of such sequences is equivalent to the set of all binary sequences that are either all '0's or start with some number of '1's followed by all '0's. The cardinality of this set is the same as the cardinality of the continuum, which is $\aleph_0$.",
"assumptions":["I chose to consider binary sequences of any length.","The problem is about the cardinality of the set of such sequences."]}

